hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2968","###\n Narrated to us Ali bin Khushram, who said: Isa informed us, from Ibn Jurayj. And narrated to us Abu Kurayb, who said: Abu Khalid informed us. [In another chain] Narrated to us Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashajj, who said: Ibn Idris informed me. [And in another chain] Narrated to us Muhammad bin Ma'mar, who said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Bakr, informed us. All of them narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said:"
"2969","###\n Muhammad bin Al-Ala narrated to us, stating: Humaid Al-Kufi (also known as Ibn Khuwar) narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: \"I do not throw (the pebbles) until the sun has risen.\" He mentioned that Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) said: \"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to throw (the pebbles) on the Day of Sacrifice before the sun declined (Zawal), but as for after that, he would do so at the time"
